// SPU instruction table: X(enum, mnemonic, form, opcode, operands...).
//
// `opcode` is the 11-bit major opcode (bits 0-10 of the word); forms with shorter
// opcodes (RRR 4 bits, RI18/LBT 7, RI10 8, RI16 9, RI8 10) give theirs in the top bits
// of those 11. Operands are listed in assembler order. Values and order follow the
// GNU binutils table (opcode/spu-insns.h); where two entries share an opcode binutils
// prints the first one, so aliases that never win (lr, bit, syscall...) are left out.
// Validated against spu-elf-objdump on every SPU program of the game (docs/SPU.md).

